{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And he saw — Issachar, the restfulness of the land." "That it was good — more than going out to distant places." "And the land that it was pleasant — and successful, as it is written: אל המנוחה ואל הנחלה." "And he bent his shoulder to bear — the yoke of the kings of Israel." "And he became a servant at forced labor — to give the kings a tithe of his produce, as it is written: ואת שדותיכם יעשור; this is the essence of the plain sense. And the tidings of wealth are for the tribe of Issachar."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:44.616594683Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}